WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.190
As upsetting as the ending to Avengers: Infinity
War was, there's a good chance that a lot

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:08.810
of the most devastating losses of the film
will be reversed when the fourth Avengers

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:10.139
movie comes along.

00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:13.869
If you haven't seen Infinity War yet, avert
your eyes now!

00:00:13.869 --> 00:00:17.980
Considering the fact that sequels for Black
Panther, Guardians of the Galaxy, and Spider-Man:

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:24.140
Homecoming have all been confirmed, the very
future of the MCU depends on a lot of Infinity

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.370
War being undone.

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:28.710
What we don't know yet is how the Russo brothers
will make that happen.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:32.929
They could do the obvious and draw directly
from the source material, but there are also

00:00:32.929 --> 00:00:37.300
other clues in Infinity War that their plan
might go in another direction.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:42.059
We won't know until May of 2019 exactly how
they do it, but here are a few of the ways

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.000
Infinity War's ending could be reversed.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.220
Daughter of mine

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:50.800
The most obvious answer to how Infinity War's
ending could be reversed is to follow the

00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:53.260
comics and leave it all up to Nebula.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:58.710
Infinity War is partly based on the 1991 comic
book mini-series Infinity Gauntlet, in which

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:03.679
Thanos collects the six Infinity Stones and
erases half the life in the universe with

00:01:03.679 --> 00:01:05.190
his infamous snap.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:08.970
In the comics, however, that all takes place
in the beginning of the story.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:13.330
Near the end, though, Nebula uses Thanos'
momentary distraction to take the gauntlet

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:17.450
from him, and one of her first actions is
to undo Thanos' actions.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:22.750
So, all the people Thanos got rid of with
his genocidal "snap", and everyone who didn't

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:26.310
survive trying to take the gauntlet from him,
are suddenly revived.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:31.710
Conveniently, Nebula has survived the battle
in Infinity War, so that option is still certainly

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:32.930
on the table.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:37.670
At the same time, though, that might seem
a little too obvious an approach for the Russos,

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:41.730
who clearly made a point of diverging from
the source material in other ways for Infinity

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:45.450
War, so let's consider some other options
as well.

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.270
They've got soul

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:51.850
There are a lot of theorists who believe we're
going to see a pretty serious soul trade go

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:53.500
down in Infinity War.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:58.810
In the comics, the Soul Stone contains an
entire world full of lost spirits, so some

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:04.740
fans suspect the victims of Infinity War's
conclusion didn't really perish but were instead

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:06.790
absorbed into the Soul Stone.

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:11.420
That could include Gamora, given her proximity
to the Stone at the moment of her demise.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:16.020
It's probably no coincidence that most of
Infinity War's survivors are core members

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:20.640
of the Avengers whose actor counterparts plan
to make this their final Marvel movie.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:25.230
Just as Thanos had to pay the price of Gamora's
life to get the Stone, if the Stone contains

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:30.090
the souls of Thanos' victims, then it may
mean some horrible price will have to be paid

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:34.110
to free those victims, and who better to do
that than the team that first assembled to

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:36.810
save the universe in the first place.

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.500
Vision of the future

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:43.510
Seconds before Corvus Glaive breaks through
to the lab in Wakanda, Shuri stops her work

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:48.420
on Vision to very quickly type something into
the display before throwing on her gloves

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.190
and attacking Corvus.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:54.680
And since she didn't separate Vision from
the Mind Stone, one has to assume that whatever

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:57.670
she was doing, it wasn't finishing that job.

00:02:57.670 --> 00:03:02.450
One idea is that Shuri was actually backing
up Vision's consciousness just in case the

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:04.060
inevitable happened.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:08.440
If he's not trapped in the Soul Stone with
the rest, due to the fact that he might not

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:13.319
have a soul in the traditional sense, well,
he might still be with us in another form

00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:14.530
or fashion.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:18.319
If that's the case, then the Avengers might
have an ace up their sleeve they don't know

00:03:18.319 --> 00:03:19.319
about.

00:03:19.319 --> 00:03:23.230
By preserving Vision's digital consciousness,
the team may learn some secrets about the

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:25.790
Stones that even Thanos doesn't know.

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:30.620
After all, Vision did mention feeling like
the Stone was talking to him, so perhaps after

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:35.120
being freed from its intensity, his backed-up
mind will be clearer and able to give the

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:39.340
Avengers the information they need to reverse
Thanos' work.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:40.920
Here she comes

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:44.390
Captain Marvel is coming, and she may be the
key to everything.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:48.610
The Carol Danvers of the MCU will be different
from the comics' version of the character.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:54.640
Marvel boss Kevin Feige has said Captain Marvel
is easily the strongest all the MCU heroes,

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:58.739
whereas in the comics, tons of heroes would
technically beat her in that department.

00:03:58.739 --> 00:04:03.400
We also know Josh Brolin has confirmed he's
filmed scenes with Brie Larson for Avengers

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:08.310
4, so if the post-credits scene wasn't enough
of a confirmation, we know for sure that she'll

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:10.510
be in the movie and fighting Thanos.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:14.090
When Nick Fury saw what was happening, Captain
Marvel wasn't one of his calls.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:19.340
It was his only call, which suggests that
Fury knew she was the one for the job.

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:23.910
We won't know the full of extent of her abilities
until Avengers 4, or whether they have anything

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:28.530
to do with the reversal, but however Thanos
bites the dust, she'll be giving him one of

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.490
his biggest bites.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.160
His own worst enemy

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.601
In the end, the one who reverses his "victory"
may be Thanos itself.

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:41.160
It's been often commented in the comics that
Thanos is the cause of his many defeats.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:45.460
Time and again, the Mad Titan has grasped
limitless power that should have allowed him

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:48.900
to brush aside all challengers, but still
he failed.

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:53.889
But saying Thanos is his own worst enemy may
prove to be more than cliché or metaphor.

00:04:53.889 --> 00:04:58.580
Right before he sacrifices Gamora, he tells
her that he ignored his destiny once and that

00:04:58.580 --> 00:04:59.910
he can't do it again.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:04.660
Of course, we didn't get to see whatever missed
moment he was talking about before, but perhaps

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:06.530
his daughter Nebula did.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:11.600
Time travel is expected to play a big role
in Avengers 4, so if there was a time when

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:16.830
Thanos "ignored" his insane crusade to slaughter
half the universe, perhaps Nebula can lead

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:22.190
everyone to it and figure out how to recruit
that version of him to join the war against

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:23.190
himself?

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:25.490
Crazier things have happened.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:26.850
Dream a little dream

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:31.650
It might seem cheap at first, but the idea
that everything in the Infinity War was some

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:34.910
kind of sick dream isn't completely unsupported.

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:37.870
Think back when Thanos acquired the Soul Stone.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:42.400
After Thanos throws Gamora from the edge of
the cliff as the ultimate sacrifice of someone

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:48.260
he loves, a bright light issues from the sky
above Thanos and envelopes everything.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:52.760
Then Thanos blacks out and awakens somewhere
else with the Soul Stone in hand.

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:55.820
Perhaps that exact moment is when his plan
has gone awry.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:06:01.030
What if Gamora was right and Thanos didn't
actually love anything enough to earn the

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:02.030
stone?

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:06.750
If so, Thanos waking up in a different place
may have indicated that he failed the test

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:12.051
and was instead in the interior of the Soul
Stone, dreaming out his supposed fate as the

00:06:12.051 --> 00:06:13.640
master of the universe.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:17.720
It's pretty unlikely, but we'll have to wait
to find out for sure next year when Avengers

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:18.930
4 hits theaters.

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:20.199
Thanks for watching!

00:06:20.199 --> 00:06:22.720
